# Day 35

**14km / 5 hours**

Felt a bit more determined this morning despite the steady rain coming down. There was a short road walk before turning off to the well formed track alongside a stream. This was very comfortable even when it was raining since it involved a wide path with very gentle inclines.

![The nice stream I was walking besides](./stream.avif)

Slowly the track became more arduous as it winded upwards, becoming more steep and slippery. Sections of mud and tree roots dominated the narrower path, making progress slower. As the trees cleared and other plants dominated with the higher altitude I was sure that I was nearing the summit. The track was almost a stream at this point from the extreme amount of water flowing down it and the wind was biting without the protection from the trees. I struggled onwards. 

Surely the summit and hut for shelter were near was my overriding thought throughout this section. It was too wet to take my phone out to check but surely I had been travelling for hours and had to be just about to get to the summit. I kept going. 

Finally after what seemed like forever, I came to a sign which said 2km/1 hour to the hut. How could that be? Nothing to do but grit my teeth and push forward. At this point there was more boardwalk which was hugely appreciated since it meant less trudging through mud and done quicker progress. I passed the actual summit with a lookout and signs but there was no point in going up the lookout since the only view would've been white clouds.

Artist's rendition of the view -> ⚪

Didn't feel like long before I came to the campsite and hut which was a huge relief. I took off most of the soaking wet clothes and got into warm, dry ones. It was around noon so I tucked into lunch food from my bag while I evaluated what to do next. I had planned to go further today but sitting dry inside a nice hut while swirling winds and pouring rain fell outside dampened my enthusiasm for that. Eventually after some deliberation (read: indecisiveness) I just decided to stay put. It was a shorter day but I could use it after the last few and I had sufficient food for it. 

![The magnificent hut standing strong against the wind and rain](./hut.avif)

There was a lot of waiting around in the hut but it was nice watching the weather slowly improve. It was still windy but the cloud was a little nicer and the rain went away. Really hoping for better weather tomorrow.